# Onboarding and vault routing

This Cursor rule supplements the repository AGENTS.md instructions. It may add scoped requirements but may not weaken root security invariants.

**Authority:** [`apps/web/AGENTS.md`](../../apps/web/AGENTS.md) · [`security-invariants.mdc`](security-invariants.mdc) · [`core-and-worker.mdc`](core-and-worker.mdc)

## Do not

- Expose create/import setup UI when a vault already exists — redirect to `/unlock` or `/wallet`
- Send backup flow to generic `/onboarding` when a vault exists — check vault and session first
- Pass backup mnemonics via `sessionStorage`, URL params, or Zustand — use React Router `location.state` only
- Use `loadVaultMetadata()` alone for routing decisions on the main thread — use `hasVault()` or `getVaultMetadata()` per [`core-and-worker.mdc`](core-and-worker.mdc)
- Navigate to wallet routes after reset without `replace: true`

## Pattern anchors

### BAD

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!mnemonic) navigate("/onboarding", { replace: true });
}, [mnemonic]);
```

### GOOD

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!mnemonic) {
    void hasVault().then((exists) => {
      if (!exists) {
        navigate("/onboarding/create", { replace: true });
        return;
      }
      const unlocked = useSessionStore.getState().isUnlocked;
      navigate(unlocked ? "/wallet" : "/unlock", { replace: true });
    });
  }
}, [mnemonic, navigate]);
```
